  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One credential, one seal",
      "items": [
        "Credential Manager (passkeys, passwords, Google) or AppAuth + Custom Tabs with PKCE: the app never sees a password",
        "the token is sealed by Keystore + Tink and read back through a TokenProvider port — never SharedPreferences, Room, logs or the APK",
        "a token in SharedPreferences is a breach on a shared device, and that is why the vault is a separate boundary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The server decides",
      "items": [
        "the token exchange verifies PKCE and state server-side; the client never decides access",
        "Play Integrity is a server-side risk signal: the verdict informs the server's decision, it is never a client block",
        "a 403 is a rendered state (UiState.Forbidden), not an empty screen — every state is rendered"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Sign-out",
      "items": [
        "revoke the refresh token server-side first, then delete the Keystore key and clear the local user data",
        "the FCM token is revoked on logout too; a deep link received while signed out is queued and resumed after login",
        "clear user data on sign-out or tenant switch, pending outbox rows included"
      ]
    }
  ]
